@startuml websocket_connection_scope_comparison
title WebSocket Connection Scope Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: 91dca69dae23d3bdeff5aefb8400249a04216039
' Source: docs/gateway/protocol.md (Gateway protocol, broadcast scope)
' Source: packages/gateway-protocol/src/schema/logs-chat.ts (ChatSendParamsSchema, ChatEventSchema)
' Source: src/gateway/server-broadcast.ts (createGatewayBroadcaster)
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ServerMode.java (configureRoutes)
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java (handle)
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/SessionPool.java (getOrCreate)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/README.md (WebSocket v2 target)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw uses one Gateway connection for requests and events across sessions.
' Current Java behavior: one connection captures one AgentSession selected by a query parameter.
' Target design: one CampusClaw connection is bound to one agent and conversation after connect.
' Design reason: Session scope fixes authorization, model, disclosure, and audit boundaries.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
left to right direction

package "OpenClaw - implemented" as openclaw {
  actor "Gateway client" as oc_client
  component "Gateway connection" as oc_conn
  component "Gateway control plane" as oc_gateway
  database "Session A" as oc_session_a
  database "Session B" as oc_session_b
  component "Node and control APIs" as oc_control

  oc_client --> oc_conn
  oc_conn --> oc_gateway : req/res/event
  oc_gateway --> oc_session_a : sessionKey=A
  oc_gateway --> oc_session_b : sessionKey=B
  oc_gateway --> oc_control : methods and events
}

package "pi-mono-java v1 - current" as java_v1 {
  actor "Chat client" as java_client
  component "WebSocket connection" as java_conn
  component "ChatWebSocketHandler" as java_handler
  database "AgentSession" as java_session
  database "SessionPool\nkey: conversation_id" as java_pool

  java_client --> java_conn : query conversation_id
  java_conn --> java_handler
  java_handler --> java_pool
  java_pool --> java_session
}

package "CampusClaw v2 - target only" as campus_v2 {
  actor "Chat client" as cc_client
  component "Session-scoped connection" as cc_conn
  component "ManagedSessionPool" as cc_pool
  component "ManagedRunHub" as cc_hub
  database "Agent A / Conversation 1" as cc_session
  actor "Observer client" as cc_observer

  cc_client --> cc_conn : connect once
  cc_observer --> cc_conn : another subscription
  cc_conn --> cc_pool : agent_id + conversation_id
  cc_pool --> cc_session
  cc_session --> cc_hub : zero or one active run
}

note bottom of openclaw
  One connection may address many sessions.
  Subscription and scope filters still apply.
end note

note bottom of java_v1
  Session identity is not agent-qualified.
  new_session changes the captured session.
end note

note bottom of campus_v2
  The binding cannot change after connect.
  A new conversation uses a new connection.
end note
@enduml

@startuml websocket_handshake_comparison
title WebSocket Handshake and Authentication Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: 91dca69dae23d3bdeff5aefb8400249a04216039
' Source: docs/gateway/protocol.md (Handshake, authentication, protocol versioning)
' Source: docs/gateway/clients.md (scopes, pairing, capabilities)
' Source: packages/gateway-protocol/src/schema/frames.ts (ConnectParamsSchema, HelloOkSchema)
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ServerMode.java (configureRoutes)
' Source: docs/asyncapi/chat-ws.yaml (query parameters and v1 messages)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw emits a challenge before the first client connect frame.
' Current Java behavior: the route reads conversation_id and creates or resumes a session immediately.
' Target design: CampusClaw authenticates the Upgrade and then requires connect within five seconds.
' Design reason: enterprise credentials stay in transport authentication and never enter chat payloads.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
autonumber

actor "OpenClaw client" as OC
participant "OpenClaw Gateway" as OG
actor "Java v1 client" as JV1C
participant "ServerMode" as SM
participant "ChatWebSocketHandler" as CWH
actor "CampusClaw client" as CC
participant "HTTP auth edge" as EDGE
participant "Chat v2 endpoint" as V2
participant "Agent and Model Managers" as MGR

== OpenClaw implemented ==
OC -> OG : WebSocket Upgrade
OG --> OC : event connect.challenge {nonce, ts}
OC -> OG : req connect {minProtocol, maxProtocol,\nauth, device, role, scopes, caps}
OG --> OC : res hello-ok {protocol, policy, snapshot}
note over OC,OG
The challenge is a server event.
The first client frame is connect.
Device identity and pairing support broad Gateway access.
end note

== pi-mono-java v1 current ==
JV1C -> SM : Upgrade /api/ws/chat?conversation_id=...
SM -> CWH : handle(exchange, conversationId)
CWH --> JV1C : WebSocket accepted; no protocol hello
note over JV1C,CWH
The v1 AsyncAPI documents a token query parameter.
The baseline route shown here extracts only conversation_id.
There is no connect protocol negotiation.
end note

== CampusClaw v2 target only ==
CC -> EDGE : Upgrade /api/ws/chat\nCookie or Authorization Bearer
EDGE -> EDGE : validate Origin and identity consistency
EDGE -> V2 : immutable authenticated connection context
CC -> V2 : req connect within 5 seconds\n{min_protocol, max_protocol,\nagent_id, conversation_id?, model_id?}
V2 -> MGR : authorize agent and resolve model
MGR --> V2 : effective identity and model
V2 --> CC : res connect {protocol, connection_id,\nsession, limits, active_run?}
note over CC,V2
No business query parameter and no URL token.
The connection cannot switch agent or conversation.
end note
@enduml

@startuml websocket_stream_recovery_comparison
title Stream and Recovery Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: 91dca69dae23d3bdeff5aefb8400249a04216039
' Source: src/gateway/server-chat.ts (resolveBroadcastDelta, emitChatDelta, sequence gap handling)
' Source: src/gateway/server-broadcast.ts (createGatewayBroadcaster, per-client seq, slow consumers)
' Source: ui/src/pages/chat/chat-gateway.ts (resolveAssistantTextFromChatEvent)
' Source: ui/src/app/gateway-store.ts (sequence gap reconnect)
' Source: docs/gateway/clients.md (recovery, chat.history, inFlightRun)
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java (mapEventToJson, close handling)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/README.md (ManagedRunHub)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw clients recover from sequence gaps by reconnecting and reloading authoritative state.
' Current Java behavior: message_update sends the accumulated message and disconnect aborts streaming.
' Target design: ManagedRunHub owns the run and atomically returns a snapshot plus a post-cursor stream.
' Design reason: network connection lifetime must not define model run lifetime.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
autonumber

actor "OpenClaw client" as OC
participant "Gateway broadcaster" as OGB
participant "Chat history" as OCH
actor "Java v1 client" as JVC
participant "ChatWebSocketHandler" as JWH
participant "AgentSession" as JAS
actor "CampusClaw client" as CCC
participant "Chat v2 connection" as CCW
participant "ManagedRunHub" as MRH
participant "Session history" as CCH

== OpenClaw implemented ==
OGB --> OC : chat event {seq, runId, sessionKey,\ndeltaText, message?, replace?}
OGB --> OC : later event with sequence gap
OC -> OC : detect connection or run sequence gap
OC -> OCH : chat.history(sessionKey)
OCH --> OC : authoritative messages and in-flight state
note over OC,OGB
Some chat deltas may be marked dropIfSlow.
A gap is observable because sequence numbers advance.
end note

== pi-mono-java v1 current ==
JAS --> JWH : MessageUpdateEvent(fullMessage, fineGrainedEvent)
JWH --> JVC : message_update {message: fullMessage}
JVC -x JWH : connection closes
JWH -> JAS : abort()
note over JVC,JAS
The wire format does not expose the fine-grained event.
There is no active-run snapshot protocol.
end note

== CampusClaw v2 target only ==
MRH --> CCW : message.updated {run_seq, typed delta}
CCW --> CCC : current delta only
CCC -x CCW : connection closes
note over MRH
The run continues without a WebSocket subscriber.
end note
CCC -> CCW : reconnect and req connect
CCW -> MRH : atomically subscribe and capture cursor
MRH --> CCW : active_run snapshot at run_seq=N
CCW --> CCC : connect response with full partial message and tools
MRH --> CCW : deltas after N
CCW --> CCC : ordered message.updated events
CCC -> CCH : chat.history if the run ended while offline
CCH --> CCC : authoritative completed messages
@enduml
